WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.700
HBO just announced on Game of Thrones official
Twitter account that Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.000
series, House of the Dragon will begin filming
with the start of 2021.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.610
Beside this announcement, they also teased
two dragon concept arts of the dragons

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.369
that are going to play a major role in this
prequel

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:32.710
and those dragons are Aegon II's Sunfyre and
Daemon's Caraxes.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.559
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:40.990
to air in 2022.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:45.829
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:50.320
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.929
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:54.929 --> 00:01:00.039
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:04.390
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:10.320
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:15.520
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.520
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
The key event of the prequel will be the Dance

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.770
of the Dragon, a Targaryen civil war.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.000
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.960
producer.
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:38.700
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.
A war of succession between Aegon II and his

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.860
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys
I's throne.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.790
Both of them thought they belonged on the
Iron Throne. When people started declaring

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:51.990
for one of them or the other, their fight
divided the kingdoms in two. Targaryens fought

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:57.460
Targaryens, bothers fought brothers, dragons
fought dragons. By the time it was over, thousands

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:01.660
were dead. The conflict would prove to be
incredibly destructive for not only House

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:07.180
Targaryen, but large parts of Westeros as
well. In addition, it devastated the Targaryen's

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:11.200
dragon population, ultimately leading to their
extinction within a few decades.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.580
They never truly recovered.
By the end of the reign of King Viserys I

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:19.870
Targaryen, twenty dragons were alive. The
majority of these died during the civil war

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:27.700
called the Dance of the Dragons, which began
in 129 AC and lasted until mid 131 AC.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.069
The dragon that played a huge role in this
Targaryen civil war was Ceraxes,

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:35.640
one of the dragons HBO shared its concept
art.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.980
Caraxes was the dragon ridden by Prince Daemon
Targaryen during the Dance of the Dragons.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:45.980
A veteran of many battles, he was known as
the Blood Wyrm for his red scales.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:50.480
Caraxes was one of the older and larger dragons
during the Dance of the Dragons.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.450
Daemon Targaryen rode Caraxes in his frequent
campaigns in the Stepstones.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.180
As a result Caraxes was not only one of the
larger dragons during the Dance,

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:03.310
but the most battle-hardened and experienced
in war.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:08.239
Indeed, only Vhagar had ever been ridden in
major wars before, during Aegon's Conquest,

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:12.720
but while formidable, Vhagar had not been
used in combat in the years leading up to

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.640
the Dance,
the way that Caraxes was.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:20.819
Opposing armies were known to often simply
flee or surrender when Caraxes approached.

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:25.209
When Rhaenyra captured King's Landing in a
surprise attack, Daemon rode Caraxes in the

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:29.069
assault
while Rhaenyra rode Syrax. Later in the war,

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:35.579
Aegon II's younger brother Aemond Targaryen
resorted to a one-man war riding Vhagar, burning

00:03:35.579 --> 00:03:40.519
out much of the Riverlands.
Daemon hunted him for a long time on Caraxes,

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:45.709
aided by other dragonriders and their dragons,
but eventually he returned alone to Harrenhal

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:52.060
waiting as a challenge for Aemond to arrive.
Caraxes was formidable, but Vhagar was twice

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:57.269
his size, nearly as large as Balerion had
been during the War of Conquest. Facing him

00:03:57.269 --> 00:04:00.129
alone was the only way for Daemon to draw
Vhagar out,

00:04:00.129 --> 00:04:06.139
however, as Aemond had avoided ambushes by
multiple other dragons. Aemond arrived,

00:04:06.139 --> 00:04:11.659
exchanged his final challenges to Daemon,
then both took to the air on their dragons.

00:04:11.659 --> 00:04:15.809
The resulting Battle Above the Gods Eye was
one of the most epic dragon-versus-dragon

00:04:15.809 --> 00:04:20.320
fights of the entire civil war, as two of
the greatest living dragons fought in the

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.510
air.
Their shrieks shattered every remaining window

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.150
in the castle and could be heard for miles
around.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.490
Their fire-breath filled the sky so that fishermen
in the lake thought that the whole sky was

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:34.849
aflame.
In the end, Caraxes dove down from the sun

00:04:34.849 --> 00:04:38.690
on Aemond's blind side (due to his missing
eye).

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:42.759
Caraxes slammed into Vhagar and they both
continued to fight in free fall.

00:04:42.759 --> 00:04:48.710
Vhagar tore out Caraxes's belly, and used
her massive jaws to rip one of his wing-arms

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:54.289
completely off - but Caraxes sank his teeth
into Vhagar's throat and maintained a death

00:04:54.289 --> 00:04:57.840
grip.
As the two dragons grappled, Daemon rose from

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:03.800
his saddle and made stunning mid-air leap
from his dragon to Aemond on Vhagar's back.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:09.020
Wielding the Valyrian steel sword Dark Sister
(which had once been carried by Vhagar's previous

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:14.479
rider, Visenya Targaryen, Daemon thrust his
blade through Aemond's empty eye socket - the

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:19.840
force of his impact as he landed driving the
sword through the back of Aemond's head. Both

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:26.020
dragons plummeted into Gods Eye below. Both
dragons and both dragonriders died.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:31.349
Daemon's corpse was never found, but Aemond's
was found years later with Dark Sister still

00:05:31.349 --> 00:05:37.090
thrust through its skull. The battle was a
heavy blow for both Rhaenyra's and Aegon II's

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:40.610
factions:
each side lost one of their greatest champions,

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:46.169
as well as each side's strongest dragon.
The other dragon concept art HBO shared is

00:05:46.169 --> 00:05:50.740
for Sunfyre. Sunfyre, known as Sunfyre the
Golden,

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:56.010
was the mount of Aegon II Targaryen during
the Dance of the Dragons. According to some

00:05:56.010 --> 00:06:00.570
sources, Sunfyre was the most beautiful dragon
ever seen upon the earth.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:05.970
Sunfyre had gleaming gold scales and his flames
were golden as well.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:10.659
Sunfyre was a relatively young dragon. He
was not considered one of the "large" dragons

00:06:10.659 --> 00:06:16.020
like Caraxes. At the same time he was very
much at the upper end of the "medium" dragons,

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:21.820
very strong and formidable in combat. As the
conflict between Aegon and Rhaenyra intensified

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:28.310
into full scale war, Aegon II grew increasingly
impatient with his grandfather Otto Hightower's

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:33.199
diplomatic maneuverings, and wanted to launch
an immediate attack on Rhaenyra's followers

00:06:33.199 --> 00:06:38.300
on the mainland. With Lord Commander Criston
Cole, he launched a campaign into the east

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:42.340
of the Crownlands.
This culminated in the siege of Rook's Rest,

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:47.840
when Rhaenys Targaryen arrived riding the
large older dragon Meleys to attempt to lift

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.470
the siege of the castle. This was all a trap,
however,

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:55.099
as the Greens had kept two of their own dragons
hidden and in reserve

00:06:55.099 --> 00:07:01.009
so they could take Meleys in an uneven fight.
Aegon II appeared riding the younger, but

00:07:01.009 --> 00:07:07.069
strong Sunfyre, and his younger brother Aemond
Targaryen also attacked riding massive Vhagar,

00:07:07.069 --> 00:07:12.099
the last of the first generation Targaryen
dragons. Rhaenys could not prevail against

00:07:12.099 --> 00:07:18.039
such odds, yet she did not flee,
but flew head-on to meet her attackers. Meleys

00:07:18.039 --> 00:07:23.629
was still so large and powerful that she put
up a brutal fight. When the dust settled Meleys

00:07:23.629 --> 00:07:29.539
was dead and Vhagar was relatively unharmed,
but Sunfyre had been nearly killed and permanently

00:07:29.539 --> 00:07:33.000
maimed.
Meleys managed to nearly rip one of his wing-arms

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:37.319
completely from his body,
and as for Aegon II, he was left horrifically

00:07:37.319 --> 00:07:43.160
burned and with multiple broken bones.
Aegon II was taken back to King's Landing,

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:48.310
but he was left sedated with milk of the poppy
for months, and command fell to his younger

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:53.510
brother Aemond. Sunfyre survived the battle,
but the world's most beautiful living dragon

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:58.389
was left crippled and heavily scarred, just
like its rider, Aegon.

00:07:58.389 --> 00:08:03.881
Yet even after Rhaenyra captured King's Landing,
her forces could not find Sunfyre, nor Aegon.

00:08:03.881 --> 00:08:09.189
Aegon II escaped King's Landing to hide out
as a disguised commoner

00:08:09.189 --> 00:08:14.240
in a fishing village on Dragonstone island
- the last place that Rhaenyra would search.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.360
Sunfyre also subsequently flew to Dragonstone
after he gained enough strength to fly.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:24.280
When Sunfyre arrived he fought and killed
a remaining riderless dragon, Grey Ghost –

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:29.659
although he took yet more wounds in the process.
When Aegon finally rode Sunfyre again

00:08:29.659 --> 00:08:34.310
he was attacked by Daemon's young daughter
Baela riding the dragon Moondancer –

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:39.539
an even younger dragon barely large enough
to carry the 13 year old girl.

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:44.630
Moondancer was quick, however, while Sunfyre
was still half-crippled and slowed by his

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.570
injuries.
Therefore they were evenly matched and their

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:53.690
duel was ferocious. It culminated when Sunfyre
tackled Moondancer in mid-air and drove her

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:57.589
into the ground below:
his larger size meant that he survived the

00:08:57.589 --> 00:09:01.810
fall while she was killed.
Nonetheless Sunfyre was mortally injured by

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:06.639
this fight, and would never fly again.
When Rhaenyra was forced to flee King's Landing

00:09:06.639 --> 00:09:11.560
due to a city-wide riot,
she returned to Dragonstone only to be surprised

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:17.140
and confronted by her half-brother.
Aegon II then had Rhaenyra fed to his dragon

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.530
Sunfyre
while forcing her last remaining son to watch

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:25.700
(Aegon III Targaryen).
The dragon roasted her alive and devoured

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:30.120
her in six bites. Six weeks after this, Sunfyre
died.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.150
Despite being one of the younger dragons in
the Dance,

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:37.250
Sunfyre actually shared the highest dragon
versus dragon kill count with the massive

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:41.730
Vhagar herself:
two individual kills and one assisted.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:45.490
Both Sunfyre and Vhagar died as a result of
their third dragon fights.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:50.190
For that matter, they were the only two dragons
in the Dance who ever lived through a dragon

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:55.230
versus dragon fight and lived (most dragons
in the war were actually killed by human armies,

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:59.630
or died in mutual kills in their first battle
against another dragon).

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:04.650
So many dragons had died in the war that the
Targaryens could not maintain a stable breeding

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:08.720
population, and few survivors became inbred
and sickly.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:13.350
Lots of dragons, a lot of epic dragon battles,
all of that and more this Game of Thrones

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:18.010
prequel series, House of the Dragons brings
in 2022 on HBO.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:21.490
Let me know your thoughts about everything:
the prequel, its characters,

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:25.500
the mighty dragons and their epic battles
in the comment section down below.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.570
Thank you so much for watching and hope to
see you in the next one.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:27.571
Peace!

